  "body": "When registering with an existing Gitlab/Github/Facebook/Google/Apple account, it seems like it is not possible to do any of the following:\r\n\r\n- Log in normally with email or username\r\n- Reset password\r\n\r\nThis makes sense, because both of these things are done via the existing Gitlab/Github/Facebook/Google/Apple account.  But it should then be possible to kind of \"switch\" to logging in \"normally\" with email or username and a password, and disassociate/unlink the Gitlab/Github/Facebook/Google/Apple account.\r\n\r\nOr is there already a way to do this via the API?\r\n\r\nIt is true that there is the possibility to register a new account \"normally\", and do an account transfer, but this way, one doesn't keep ones username.",
